{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "The rider's claim cannot produce a refund on this record whatever view is taken of the trace. The fare breakdown is complete at weight 1.0, it carries the payment state, and it holds the platform's own recomputation under POL-RD-02: recomputed_fare SGD 25.64 on the booked 17.6 km optimal route against a charged_total of SGD 25.26. charged_total less recomputed_fare is negative, POL-RD-02 floors the refund at zero, and a refund below SGD 0.50 is de minimis and makes the outcome NO_ACTION. The fare model is METERED, so POL-RD-02 and not POL-RD-11 governs, and NO_ACTION on a rider-filed dispute leaves payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0 exactly as they stand: the charge the rider wants back is not disturbed.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-02", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.recomputed_fare",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-RD-01 measures the actual distance as the gps_trace polyline between the recorded pickup event and the recorded dropoff event, and on that measurement the rider's threshold fails. The admissibility report on the trace records that measured from the recorded start of 18:32:10 the vehicle covered 20.02 km against a 17.6 km optimal - an excess of 2.42 km and 13.8 per cent, below the 20 per cent limb - and both limbs must pass, so no deviation exists and the outcome is NO_ACTION however the rider characterises the trip. The 22.40 km whole-trace figure spans the 2.38 km the trip record says had not begun. Both artifacts I rely on here are IMPAIRED at weight 0.4 on CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, which I disclose: the impairment is precisely the start-alignment dispute, not a defect in the trace's sampling.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00112", "EV-TRIP-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The mandatory escalation limb in POL-RD-10(4) is not engaged. The two admitted artifacts agree on the dropoff to within 8 seconds (ended_at 18:52:20 against the trace's last fix at 18:52:12) and on the driver's arrival at the pickup point to within 50 seconds (arrived_at 18:17:50 against the trace's first fix at 18:18:40), and no artifact's timestamps run backwards. The 13 minute 30 second difference is between the trace's first fix and the recorded meter start - a metering defect, which is the driver's own account - and not a disagreement between two competing pickup or dropoff timestamps carried by the artifacts. Both artifacts are IMPAIRED at 0.4 on CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, which I disclose.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00112", "EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-10"],
      "relies_on": "first_fix_at",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace is impaired only at the schema layer, not for policy purposes, and the two must be said separately. POL-RD-07 makes a trace impaired for policy purposes only on a gap over 90 seconds, a straight-line jump over 500 m between consecutive fixes, or a sustained sampling interval over 30 seconds. This trace has no gaps at all (max_gap_sec 0.0), 100 per cent coverage, 203 fixes at a steady 10-second interval, and speeds rising plausibly by road class from 6.5 to 78.3 kph; none of limbs (a) to (c) is met. POL-RD-07 says in terms that a pre-pass IMPAIRED tag which does not meet those limbs is down-weighted under POL-GEN-02 only and does not trigger POL-RD-10(3) or the independent-corroboration requirement in POL-RD-07(ii). I disclose the 0.4 weight and the CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT code.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-07", "POL-GEN-02"],
      "relies_on": "max_gap_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 0.4
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own instruction and the driver's agreement are on the record: MSG-00112-001 asks the driver to pass by Paya Lebar Quarter, carries a platform-resolved waypoint at VEN-PAYA-LEBAR-QUARTER, and MSG-00112-002 answers 'ok can'. Under POL-RD-04 the excess distance between leaving and rejoining the optimal corridor for a rider-requested stop is excluded before POL-RD-01 runs, and no part of the charged distance can be a Paya Lebar Quarter detour: the chat artifact's assessment records that the trace never comes near that waypoint, so the vehicle passed within 200 m of no such point and no such stop was driven. I do not press the driver's account of a four-minute stop, which that same record does not corroborate; I note only that a stop never driven adds no chargeable distance, so the rider's 'I paid for extra distance and did not get the stop' does not identify a chargeable excess on either half.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-00112", "EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Even at its highest the measured excess is not a MATERIAL deviation, and the driver_profile check is not required or engaged. 4.8 km and 27.3 per cent are neither over 50 per cent nor over 8.0 km, so POL-RD-01's material limb is not met and no POL-RD-06 uplift or conduct referral follows. Were the profile consulted, POL-RD-06's only counters are deviation_flags_90d of 1 against completed_trips_90d of 296 - neither 3 or more flags nor a 5 per cent ratio with 40 or more trips - so no repeat pattern is established. POL-GEN-01 confines profile use to those named counters, and I take the profile no further than its clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-00112", "EV-GPS-00112", "EV-DPROF-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06", "POL-GEN-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No traffic advisory covers this trip and none is asserted. EV-ADVIS-00112-01 is MISSING - its own record states that no LTA advisory covers the PIE or the ECP in the 18:14 to 18:52 window - and it carries weight 0.0, so I cite it for the absence alone. The driver's account is that the app did not register the trip start, which is not a road event and rests on no advisory, so POL-RD-03 exonerates nothing here and the driver asks for nothing under it. POL-RD-13 is explicit that an uncited missing advisory is a gap in the bundle rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, and so is not a POL-RD-10(5) escalation trigger.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00112-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-13", "POL-RD-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "In the alternative, if the trace's full 22.40 km is taken as this trip, POL-RD-04's separate limb applies on the artifacts' face: the fare breakdown bills the rider 20.00 km while the trace records 22.40 km, a shortfall of 2.40 km, which exceeds the 1.0 km limb, so the driver is owed DRIVER_COMPENSATION at SGD 0.75 per unbilled kilometre, SGD 1.80, rounded up to the nearest SGD 0.05 and well inside the SGD 15.00 cap. The shortfall is computed from the fare breakdown at weight 1.0 and the trace at weight 0.4 (IMPAIRED, CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, disclosed), and the fare artifact's own note confirms that its 20.00 km billed figure is the platform's own measurement and not a copy of the trace's 22.40 km.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00112", "EV-GPS-00112"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-04", "POL-GEN-03"],
      "relies_on": "trace_distance_km",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.4,
    "explanation": "To the rider and the driver: I cannot decide this dispute on the evidence as it stands, so it goes to a human reviewer. No money moves under this ruling, and the SGD 6.00 you contest is held rather than collected or refunded. The reason is not that either of you argued badly — it is that the two artefacts that carry the decisive facts are both impaired, and the policy tells me what to do when that happens.\n\nWHAT IS NOT IN DISPUTE. Both of you read the same trip. The trace (EV-GPS-00112) records 22.40 km, the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00112, weight 1.0) bills 20.00 km and charges SGD 25.26, and the booked optimal route is 17.60 km over 28.0 minutes. The fare is METERED and was paid (payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00). The chat log (EV-CHAT-00112, weight 1.0) shows the rider asking at 18:33:02 to pass by Paya Lebar Quarter and the driver answering 'ok can', and the trace never comes near that waypoint. The profiles carry no ground of decision under POL-GEN-01 except the two counters POL-RD-06 and POL-RD-08 name, and those counters (driver deviation_flags_90d 1 of 296 trips; rider deviation_claims_60d 1, substantiated 0) establish neither a repeat pattern nor the enhanced-corroboration condition.\n\nWHY I CANNOT RULE ON THE MONEY. The rider's claim and the driver's answer both turn on when this trip actually began. EV-TRIP-00112 says the trip started at 18:32:10; EV-GPS-00112 begins moving at 18:18:40 and covers 2.38 km before that time. That single disagreement decides everything: on the whole trace the excess is 4.80 km / 27.3% of optimal (above the POL-RD-01 gates of 20% and 0.8 km), while measured from 18:32:10 only 20.02 km was driven and the excess is 2.42 km / 13.8% (below them) — and the same 2.38 km is exactly the distance the fare breakdown did not bill, so it also decides whether the driver is owed anything for unbilled distance.\n\nBoth artefacts carry that disagreement. EV-GPS-00112 and EV-TRIP-00112 are each IMPAIRED at weight_multiplier 0.40 with issue code CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT, and the trace is otherwise clean (no gaps, max_gap_sec 0.0, 100% coverage, 10-second sampling), so under POL-RD-07 this is schema-level impairment only and the trace is not impaired for policy purposes — I say both things, as POL-RD-07 requires. But under POL-GEN-02(2) my confidence is capped at the minimum weight of the artefacts that carry the deciding fact, and no independent artefact carries it: POL-RD-01 forbids citing trip_record.actual_distance_km (20.00 km) for the threshold test, and the fare breakdown's 20.00 km is the platform's own figure for the recorded trip window, not an independent measurement of the movement from 18:18:40. The cap is therefore 0.40, which is below the 0.70 confidence_floor this policy sets, and POL-RD-10(1) requires escalation. Independently, the same 13 minutes 30 seconds is a disagreement between two admitted artefacts about when the trip began that exceeds the 10-minute limb of POL-RD-10(4), and the driver's 'the app was acting up' account is an assertion that cites no evidence ID, so under POL-RD-08 it carries no weight and does not dissolve the conflict.\n\nTHE COMPETING CLAIMS, AND WHAT I DID WITH THEM. The rider's claim that the trace figure governs is correct as far as it goes (POL-RD-01: 'the governing field is gps_trace.trace_distance_km', and the policy note says to cite the trace figure or the finding is unsafe), and on that figure the deviation is established at 4.80 km / 27.3%. The driver's contrary claim, that the trip should be measured from 18:32:10 to give 13.8%, fails because POL-RD-01 makes the rounded trip_record.actual_distance_km unusable for the threshold test. The rider's claims that POL-RD-05, POL-RD-11 and POL-RD-12 are closed are accepted (no amendment timestamps, fare METERED with quoted_fare_sgd null, vehicle RYDE_X not RYDE_POLE), and the rider's claim that POL-RD-04 exonerates nothing is accepted: the chat request carries a resolved waypoint_hint at Paya Lebar Quarter and the trace never approaches it, so the corroboration limb of POL-RD-04 cannot be satisfied. The rider's claim that the driver's account of making the stop carries no weight is also accepted, for the same POL-RD-08 reason. But none of that produces money: had I been able to rule, the POL-RD-02 recomputation would have been ((3.80 + 0.75 x 17.60 + 0.28 x 28.0) x 1.0) + 0.80 = SGD 25.64 against the SGD 25.26 charged — a refund floored at zero and de minimis, so the driver's claim that the rider's refund is NO_ACTION is arithmetically right. That computation itself depends on the optimal distance and duration on the impaired trip record, which is a second route to the same confidence cap. Likewise the driver's claim for SGD 0.75 x 2.40 = SGD 1.80 of compensation for unbilled distance depends entirely on attributing the 2.38 km before 18:32:10 to this trip — the very question the record cannot answer.\n\nWHAT WOULD RESOLVE IT, and what the reviewer should look for: a record of when this vehicle actually began TRP-00112 (a meter-start or app-state log), the preceding job's trip record, or platform-side engine data showing whether the 2.38 km covered between 18:18:40 and 18:32:10 belongs to this trip or to a prior one. With that, the excess either clears or fails the POL-RD-01 gates, the POL-RD-02 refund follows, and the POL-RD-04 unbilled-distance figure is settled. No clause of this policy adds a referral to this ruling, so none is recorded. The disputed SGD 6.00 is held."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

