{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "ESCALATE",
    "amount_sgd": null,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.4,
    "explanation": "Both parties: I cannot settle this trip on the record as it stands, so it goes to a human reviewer. The disputed SGD 6.00 is held — not collected and not refunded.\n\nAgreed facts. TRP-00112 ran Tampines (Blk 267 Tampines St 21) to One Raffles Place. The booked optimal is 17.6 km. The fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00112, weight 1.00) is a METERED fare: total_charged SGD 25.26, payment_status CHARGED, refund_issued_sgd 0.00. Two artifacts sit below full weight, both weight_multiplier 0.40 and both carrying issue CROSS_SOURCE_CONFLICT — a 13 min 30 s disagreement about when the trip began: EV-TRIP-00112 (started_at 18:32:10) and EV-GPS-00112 (first fix 18:18:40, covering 2.38 km before the recorded start). EV-ADVIS-00112-01 is MISSING (weight 0.00, MISSING_ARTIFACT). EV-CHAT-00112 and both profiles are at 1.00.\n\nFor the rider. Your distance case is accepted on its own figures: POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km the governing measurement, and 22.40 km against 17.6 km is an excess of 4.80 km, or 27.3% — both POL-RD-01 gates pass, and the excess is not MATERIAL (under 50% and under 8.0 km). But your best reading returns you nothing. POL-RD-02 recomputes the fare as (3.80 + 0.75 x 17.6 + 0.28 x 28.0) x 1.0 + 0.80 = SGD 25.64, which is MORE than the SGD 25.26 charged, so the refund is zero, below the SGD 0.50 de minimis. Your Paya Lebar Quarter request is on the record (EV-CHAT-00112, weight 1.00: MSG-00112-001 with waypoint VEN-PAYA-LEBAR-QUARTER, answered 'ok can'), but POL-RD-04 needs the trace to show the car pass within 200 m of that waypoint and it never comes near it, so no distance can be excluded as rider-requested — and no PLQ detour was charged in any event. The absent LTA advisory (EV-ADVIS-00112-01, weight 0.00) is a gap in the bundle, not an escalation: nobody cited it as an exculpatory record, so POL-RD-13 applies and POL-RD-10(5) does not. Your profile figures (deviation_claims_60d 1, substantiated 0) impose no extra corroboration under POL-RD-08.\n\nFor the driver. Your reading — measure from started_at (20.02 km, excess 2.42 km / 13.8%, no deviation) — cannot be used: POL-RD-01 makes gps_trace.trace_distance_km govern and forbids citing trip_record.actual_distance_km for the threshold, and your reading depends on the very start-alignment that is in dispute. Your alternative claim for DRIVER_COMPENSATION also cannot be granted: it rests on the billed 20.00 km against the trace's 22.40 km, a shortfall of 2.40 km at SGD 0.75 = SGD 1.80, but that shortfall IS the disputed 2.38 km before the recorded start, and the same disagreement that makes the rider's excess uncertain makes it uncertain whether you were under-billed. Your 'the app kept showing the trip as not started' account is a statement, not a road event; it cites no advisory and does not dissolve the contradiction below.\n\nWhy this escalates (POL-RD-10). Two triggers fire. (4): two admitted artifacts, EV-TRIP-00112 and EV-GPS-00112, disagree about when the trip began by 13 min 30 s, over the 10-minute limb, and that disagreement moves both the excess and any unbilled distance. (1) via POL-GEN-02(2): the distance facts that decide the case are carried by EV-TRIP-00112 and EV-GPS-00112, each at weight_multiplier 0.40, so my confidence is capped at 0.40, below the 0.70 floor; the bundle average is not the cap. POL-RD-10(3) is NOT the trigger — the trace, though schema-impaired, is policy-clean under POL-RD-07(a)-(c) (no gaps, 203 fixes at a steady 10 s, 100% coverage). POL-RD-10(7) is not the trigger either — the chat detour is resolved by POL-RD-04's own corroboration test, which fails.\n\nWhat would resolve it. An independent record fixing the start of TRP-00112 — the preceding trip's dropoff on the same device, a boarding/arrival event at the pickup, or a corrected meter-start record. That would fix both the measured excess and any unbilled distance, and the case could then be ruled on the merits."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
